# Phase 20 (master directive numbering): Production Release Engineering.
# Shell scripts MUST keep LF line endings regardless of a cloning
# machine's own core.autocrlf setting -- a CRLF-corrupted shebang line
# ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") fails outright on a real Linux host ("bad
# interpreter: ...bash\r: no such file"), the actual real-world target
# for scripts/backup_postgres.sh and restore_postgres.sh. This
# project's own dev machine has core.autocrlf=true (Windows), which
# would otherwise silently store/checkout these with CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
